Building and installing libdvdcss
==================================

Requirements
------------

libdvdcss requires Meson 1.3 or newer, Ninja, a C11 compiler, and a C++23
compiler/standard library. The configure step verifies every required C++23
facility instead of relying on compiler version numbers.

Supported targets are Linux, Windows, and macOS on x86-64 or AArch64.

Native build
------------

  meson setup build --buildtype=release --prefix=/usr
  meson compile -C build
  meson test -C build --print-errorlogs
  meson install -C build

Meson builds both shared and static libraries by default. Select only one with
`-Ddefault_library=shared` or `-Ddefault_library=static`.

Set `-Denable_examples=true` to build the command-line diagnostics. The
`dvd_region` utility is Linux-only because it uses the Linux DVD ioctl ABI.

Sanitizer build
---------------

With Clang or GCC:

  meson setup build-sanitize \
    -Dbuildtype=debug \
    -Db_sanitize=address,undefined \
    -Db_lundef=false
  meson compile -C build-sanitize
  meson test -C build-sanitize --print-errorlogs

Some ptrace-based containers cannot run LeakSanitizer. In that environment,
run the last command with `ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0`; AddressSanitizer and
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer remain active.

Windows
-------

For an x86-64 MinGW-w64 cross-build:

  meson setup build-windows \
    --cross-file package/crossfiles/x86_64-w64-mingw32.meson
  meson compile -C build-windows

An AArch64 MinGW/LLVM template is provided at
`package/crossfiles/aarch64-w64-mingw32.meson`; adjust binary names for the
installed toolchain.

To run x86-64 Windows tests under Wine, append
`--cross-file package/crossfiles/wine.meson` during setup.

For MSVC, open an x64 or ARM64 Visual Studio developer shell and use the native
build commands above. Meson generates a DLL export definition containing only
the public C API.

Linux AArch64
-------------

`package/crossfiles/aarch64-linux-gnu.meson` is a template for the common GNU
cross-toolchain names:

  meson setup build-aarch64 \
    --cross-file package/crossfiles/aarch64-linux-gnu.meson
  meson compile -C build-aarch64

macOS
-----

Use the native build commands with a current Apple Clang toolchain. To select
an architecture explicitly, provide an appropriate Meson native or cross file;
the supported CPU families are `x86_64` and `aarch64`.
